@startuml
title LP-SCARA Motor Test - Main Flow Summary

actor User
participant "app_main" as Main
participant "FreeRTOS Tasks" as Tasks
participant "Shared Control State" as State
participant "Motor Hardware" as Motor
participant "Encoder / Limit Switches" as Sensors

== 1. System Startup ==

Main -> Motor: Initialize GPIO and motor PWM
Main -> Sensors: Initialize encoder interrupts
Main -> Tasks: Create background tasks

note right of Tasks
LED task
User input task
Motor control task
Encoder reporting task
Limit-switch safety task
end note

== 2. User Sets a Target ==

User -> Tasks: Enter target angle or command

alt Target angle
    Tasks -> State: Convert angle to encoder count\nand save target position
else home
    Tasks -> State: Set current and target position to zero
else release / hold
    Tasks -> State: Disable control or hold current position
end

== 3. Closed-Loop Position Control ==

loop Every 20 ms
    Sensors -> State: Encoder ISR updates current position
    Tasks -> State: Read current and target position
    Tasks -> Tasks: Calculate position error and PD output

    alt Movement is required
        Tasks -> Motor: Apply direction and PWM duty
        Motor -> Sensors: Motor movement changes encoder
    else Target reached or control disabled
        Tasks -> Motor: Stop motor
    end
end

== 4. Limit-Switch Safety ==

Sensors -> Tasks: Limit-switch ISR wakes safety task
Tasks -> State: Disable position control\nand target current position
Tasks -> Motor: Stop both motors immediately
Tasks -> User: Report pressed or released switch

@enduml
